WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.900
We're back with Stephen King.

2
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.520
Someone I have known my whole life

3
00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:08.960
and love so dearly as we all do

4
00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.010
because you've changed the course of all of our lives.

5
00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.960
You have painted in the minds of all of us

6
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.950
the greatest stories, scenarios, characters, worlds,

7
00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:20.930
and I'd love to talk to you about some of,

8
00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:23.230
all of our favorites in something we're calling,

9
00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:25.010
On The Books.

10
00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:28.450
Oh, this is gonna be like a Rorschach Test.

11
00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:32.540
Okay, Carrie, published in 1974, movie released in 1976.

12
00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:33.630
What are your thoughts?

13
00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:35.050
Well, what I remember is

14
00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.620
that when the movie rights were sold for $6,500,

15
00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:40.990
I ran out to McDonald's and bought my wife

16
00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:43.800
and I Orange Blizzard shakes.

17
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.930
Okay, that is beyond my expectations

18
00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:49.850
or dreams for what this is, that's exactly it!

19
00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:53.030
Okay, The Shining, published in 1977,

20
00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:55.210
movie released in 1980.

21
00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:57.690
Well, I didn't really like the movie that much

22
00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:01.670
but I did like the little boy that played Danny Torrance.

23
00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:04.493
And of course, since then,

24
00:01:05.547 --> 00:01:09.795
"Here's Johnny" has become associated with my name forever.

25
00:01:09.795 --> 00:01:11.410
And why did you not love the movie?

26
00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:13.290
Not to press, if you don't wanna tell me it's fine,

27
00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:14.500
but I'm curious.

28
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.090
No, the book was warm and the movie was cold.

29
00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:19.690
It was a Kubrick film and don't get me wrong,

30
00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:21.820
I love everything else the man did.

31
00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:23.490
I just didn't like that one.

32
00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:26.430
The greatest thing about it is if you're not involved,

33
00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:30.010
if it's really good, you can say that's based on my book.

34
00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:31.760
If it's really bad, you can say,

35
00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:33.314
I didn't have anything to do with it.

36
00:01:33.314 --> 00:01:35.150
(Drew laughing loudly)

37
00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:38.180
Okay, Firestarter, published in 1980,

38
00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:41.290
movie released in 1984, shot in '82.

39
00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:44.300
I thought that you were terrific in that part.

40
00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:48.850
That was very, very difficult, and you were great.

41
00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:52.290
Every time that you got ready to light a fire

42
00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:54.580
your beautiful blonde hair would blow back.

43
00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:55.930
It was great.

44
00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:56.763
That's it!

45
00:01:56.763 --> 00:01:58.070
Yup, that's the look

46
00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:00.750
I loved getting to play Charlie McGee

47
00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:02.640
more than words can ever express.

48
00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.100
And when you're seven and you think you can blow people away

49
00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.706
with a fireball, it's really empowering.

50
00:02:08.706 --> 00:02:09.539
(audience laughing)

51
00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:10.372
Yeah.

52
00:02:10.372 --> 00:02:13.080
Okay, so from Different Seasons in 1982 came,

53
00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:16.340
Stand By Me, the movie in 1986.

54
00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:19.800
What I remember about writing that was my wife

55
00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:23.010
and I were living in an old house

56
00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:25.040
that was too small for a writing room.

57
00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.210
And so there was a barn next door

58
00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:29.720
and I used to work on Stand By Me,

59
00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:31.350
which was then called, The Body,

60
00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:33.250
in my underwear because it was summer

61
00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:34.540
and it was so hot in there

62
00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:36.510
but the memories just came flooding back.

63
00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.590
Oh, I love that detail.

64
00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:41.006
That's right, The Body, of course.

65
00:02:41.006 --> 00:02:41.839
(Drew gasping)

66
00:02:41.839 --> 00:02:42.970
I love that.

67
00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:45.090
Okay, one of my personal favorites,

68
00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:46.030
they're all my favorites.

69
00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:51.030
Christine, published in 1983, movie released in 1983.

70
00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:52.260
That's a quick turnover.

71
00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:53.900
I had a Plymouth like that.

72
00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.700
It wasn't quite that year

73
00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:59.490
but it was rattly and it was breaking down.

74
00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.930
And one day when I was driving it home

75
00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:03.270
I thought to myself, you know,

76
00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:05.640
what would be really great is if the odometer

77
00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:08.020
on this thing started to run backwards

78
00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:12.370
and every time it turned past, like a fender bender

79
00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:15.540 line:15%
or a flat tire, that thing would fix itself.

80
00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.450 line:15%
And I thought, you know, that's a great story.

81
00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:19.620 line:15%
I think I wanna write that, it'll be really funny,

82
00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.960 line:15%
but it didn't turn out to be that funny after all.

83
00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:25.010
I love that, it's brilliant.

84
00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.270
Okay.

85
00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:28.660
Another book you wrote that also

86
00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:31.160
became such an incredible movie, Misery.

87
00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:34.900
Published in 1987, movie in 1990.

88
00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.360
At that time, you know, I went to autograph things

89
00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:39.960
and people would line up

90
00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.860
and they would all say the same thing,

91
00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:43.449
I'm your number one fan.

92
00:03:43.449 --> 00:03:45.250
(Drew laughing)

93
00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:48.530
I thought to myself, you can't all be my number one fan.

94
00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:51.220
Somewhere there must be a number two fan

95
00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:54.630
or a number three, but they would bring things.

96
00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:58.570
And some of them were very, very serious about

97
00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:02.090
various parts of the stories and everything,

98
00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.350
and I thought, you know,

99
00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:05.550
I would hate to be captured by one of these

100
00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:07.020
and have to write a book.

101
00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:10.830 line:15%
And then the thing just followed after.

102
00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:13.643 line:15%
I mean, it was just perfect.

103
00:04:13.643 --> 00:04:16.363 line:15%
It was like automatic writing almost.

104
00:04:17.219 --> 00:04:20.610
And a detail about your new novel, Later.

105
00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:23.010
I had an idea for a story about

106
00:04:24.952 --> 00:04:27.730
a literary agent, a woman, who was on her own

107
00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:30.420
and she had financial problems

108
00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:34.100
and she had one big client that was supposed

109
00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:38.200
to pay all the bills because her life was just falling apart

110
00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:39.990
and the guy drops dead.

111
00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:41.850
So what are you gonna do about that?

112
00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:44.570
And I held onto that idea for quite a while.

113
00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:48.310
And then I thought, what if she had a kid who could talk

114
00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:51.010
to dead people and they had to tell him the truth.

115
00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:55.340
And I thought that little boy could tell her the whole story

116
00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:57.770
and she could write it under his name.

117
00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:01.410
So I started with that and I just,

118
00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:03.410
I had such a good time with that book.

119
00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:05.480
And I hope people who read it have a good time.

120
00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:08.150
It's sort of light and tasty,

121
00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:10.570
but I think it's also scary, so.

122
00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:13.700
I just love being in your world for years

123
00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:17.760
and I'm so happy to reconnect with you.

124
00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:20.480
Well, right back at you, I love being with you

125
00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:23.050
and getting a chance to connect with you

126
00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:24.630
and see your happy face.

127
00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:28.100
And I just hope everything's going great for you.

128
00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:31.030
And I watch the show and I read your book

129
00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:33.950
and you were in Firestarter and you were in Cat's Eye.

130
00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:36.220
Now, we have a real connection, it's great.

131
00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:37.650
We really do.

132
00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:40.920
Just don't lock me up in a room and make me write a book.

133
00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:43.402
Well, I am your number one fan.

134
00:05:43.402 --> 00:05:44.264
(Stephen shrieking)

135
00:05:44.264 --> 00:05:46.600
(Drew laughing loudly)

136
00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:48.110
Oh, I love you, Stephen King.

137
00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:49.630
Thank you so much for coming here.

138
00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:52.190
Please, if you'll come on your next project

139
00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:53.550
I would be so honored.

140
00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:56.040
Later, is available now!

141
00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:59.330
It dropped, it's here and we will be-

142
00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:00.163
It's here.

143
00:06:00.163 --> 00:06:01.040 line:15%
It's here.

144
00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:03.623 line:15%
(upbeat music)

